  "body": "Current logic of endian conversion\r\n\r\n```\r\n  // convert endians\r\n  if(data && (state == RADIOLIB_ERR_NONE)) {\r\n    for(size_t i = 0; i < len; i++) {\r\n      data[i] = ((uint32_t)rplBuff[2 + i*sizeof(uint32_t)] << 24) | ((uint32_t)rplBuff[3 + i*sizeof(uint32_t)] << 16) | ((uint32_t)rplBuff[4 + i*sizeof(uint32_t)] << 8) | (uint32_t)rplBuff[5 + i*sizeof(uint32_t)];\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n```\r\n\r\ndoes snot look like an accurate one. For example,\r\n an LR2021  MAGIC PRAM value (  0x600DB002  ) gets mis-read as 0xB0025000\r\n\r\nThis PR substitutes current logic of endian conversion with GNU C standard function:\r\n\r\n```\r\n  // convert endians\r\n  if(data && (state == RADIOLIB_ERR_NONE)) {\r\n    for(size_t i = 0; i < len; i++) {\r\n      data[i] = __builtin_bswap32(rplBuff[i]);\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n```\r\n\r\n",
